+gradient 1 is 0.1.</div></div></div></div></div><h2  class = 'S0'><span>Decoding without statistics module - mean thickness</span></h2><div  class = 'S1'><span>It is fully possible to also run context decoding on maps that do not per se come from the statistics module of brainstat. In example below, we decode the mean cortical thickness map of our participants</span></div><div class="CodeBlock"><div class="inlineWrapper"><div  class = 'S2'><span style="white-space: pre"><span >[correlation, feature] = meta_analytic_decoder(mean(cortical_thickness,1), </span><span style="color: rgb(14, 0, 255);">...</span></span></div></div><div class="inlineWrapper"><div  class = 'S3'><span style="white-space: pre"><span >    </span><span style="color: rgb(167, 9, 245);">'template'</span><span >, </span><span style="color: rgb(167, 9, 245);">'fsaverage5'</span><span >);</span></span></div></div><div class="inlineWrapper"><div  class = 'S3'><span style="white-space: pre"><span >figure();</span></span></div></div><div class="inlineWrapper outputs"><div  class = 'S6'><span style="white-space: pre"><span >wc = wordcloud(feature(correlation&gt;0), correlation(correlation&gt;0));</span></span></div><div  class = 'S7'><img src="data:image/png;base64," style="height: auto;"></div></div></div><h2  class = 'S0'><span>Decoding without statistics module - decoding matlab stats results</span></h2><div  class = 'S1'><span>It is equally possible to run context decoding on maps derived from other tools. In the example below, we decode results from Matlab's build in t-tests</span></div><div class="CodeBlock"><div class="inlineWrapper"><div  class = 'S2'><span style="white-space: pre"><span >A = demographics.AGE_AT_SCAN; </span></span></div></div><div class="inlineWrapper"><div  class = 'S3'><span style="white-space: pre"><span >X = cortical_thickness(A&gt;median(A),:);</span></span></div></div><div class="inlineWrapper"><div  class = 'S3'><span style="white-space: pre"><span >Y = cortical_thickness